## Normal form and ZR/ZF scope

Use a contact-minimal, then diameter-pair-minimal triangle-free global minimizer and retain every source point, including contact-isolated points. Let `V` be the nonisolated positive-contact core and `v=|V|`.

The canonical §57 theorem is

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3,
\]

so `e+h>=2v-2` and `h>=delta>=ceil(D)` in the core ledger. This is not a full-source affine-kernel theorem. Contact-isolated coordinates add zero stress rows/columns and independent kernel directions. `C-ZRF-FULL-SOURCE` is rejected.

## Canonical state through audit.54

Audit.54 controls theorem authority.

The audit.52--53 full-core structure remains canonical:
\[
\mu_D\ge\mu_{\rm hull}+\varepsilon_*,
\qquad
R_F\ge(\kappa_{\rm fr}-o(1))D,
\qquad
\sigma_C=0,
\]
with a positive reciprocal \((2,3)\)-sparse bounded-end train graph, at least \(q-k\) outer-ended trains, global face-return quotas, and joint bulk/face separator capacity.

Audit.54 adds the first canonical source-replacement theorem whose conclusion is an actual strict decrease of the full source diameter.

### Embedded wall refill

Canonical \`C-EMBEDDED-WALL-REFILL\` applies to simple actual unit-contact walls. For pairwise interior-disjoint walls \(C_j\), let \(S_j\) be the old interior source populations and \(M_j\) the sizes of certified wall-safe unit-separated refill packets. If \(T\) is a vertex cover of every actual old diameter pair and
\[
\boxed{
\sum_jM_j\ge\sum_j|S_j|+|T|,
}
\]
then deleting \(T\cup\bigcup_jS_j\) and inserting the strictified refill packets gives a same-cardinality unit-separated source with
\[
\boxed{\operatorname{diam}A'<D.}
\]

The wall shield is exact: any packet point strictly more than one from all wall vertices is strictly unit-clear from every old source point outside that wall. Separate wall packets with disjoint interiors are jointly compatible.

In the contact-minimal representative, a single wall whose certified packet capacity reaches its interior population already contradicts contact minimality whenever one deleted interior point is contact-nonisolated.

Concrete canonical consequences:

- no actual \(7\times7\) unit square contact patch;
- no \(1/50\)-near-square actual contact perturbation of that patch;
- no consecutive affine oblique unit patch satisfying
  \[
  rs(\sin\theta-\sqrt3/2)
  >
  (2-\sqrt3/2)(r+s)-4/\sin\theta.
  \]

### Pentagon-wall-disjoint quadratic train bulk

Canonical \`C-PENTAGON-WALL-DISJOINT-BULK\` proves a finite wall-conflict thinning theorem. Put
\[
K=250,\qquad
c_K=\frac1{251^2}\left(\frac{250}{251}\right)^{500}.
\]
For any family of complete trains whose two terminal occurrences lie on physical unit pentagons, some subfamily with pairwise source-vertex-disjoint terminal pentagon walls retains
\[
\boxed{
R(\mathcal A)
\ge
c_K\left[R_{PP}-(4+K/2)P\right]_+.
}
\]

In the canonical full-core branch
\[
m_B=o(D),\qquad u_B=o(D),\qquad Q-f=o(D),
\]
the post-hull-depletion crossing bulk satisfies
\[
R_{PP}=(\Delta_2-o(1))D^2
\]
on pentagon-to-pentagon trains. Therefore there is a family \(\mathcal L\) with
\[
\boxed{
|\mathcal L|=\Omega(D),\qquad
R(\mathcal L)=\Omega(D^2),
}
\]
whose terminal physical pentagon walls are pairwise source-vertex-disjoint and whose terminal edge midpoints obey
\[
\boxed{|x_\tau-y_\tau|=\Omega(D)}
\]
for every retained train.

This is genuine collective source geometry; it is not yet a simultaneous wall motion.

### Binding fixed-wall regressions

Two regression entries now constrain the live attack.

- \`C-FIXED-WALL-ACTIVATION-REGRESSION\`: positive residual, definite phase mismatch, positive KKT stress, and mixed rigidity do not imply even one fixed-wall spare site. The regular unit pentagon remains inward-capacity-zero even after any one wall point is deleted.
- \`C-LARGE-WALL-LOCK-REGRESSION\`: arbitrarily large near-triangular unit-contact walls with quadratic interior population and positive pinned equilibrium may have no alternative same-cardinality fixed-wall packing at all.

Therefore neither positive residual nor wall size can be converted into refill capacity without another hypothesis.

## Exact remaining split

### 1. Macroscopic-container branch

One actual internal inactive chamber or exterior cap has \(\Omega(D^2)\) population/area with only \(O(D)\) perimeter/slack. Canonical hull stability and deep isolate matching remain available.

The new refill theorem gives a precise sufficient endpoint: certify one or more actual unit-contact walls whose **packing surplus** pays an actual diameter vertex cover. Merely showing small positive residual is not enough.

### 2. Full-core branch

Every sufficiently large survivor has the audit.52--53 residual/contact/return structure.

A new exact subbranch is now isolated. If
\[
m_B=o(D),\qquad u_B=o(D),\qquad Q-f=o(D),
\]
then the source contains a macroscopic family of macroscopically long stopped trains with pairwise source-vertex-disjoint terminal physical pentagon walls and quadratic retained crossing mass.

The live theorem is therefore:

\[
\boxed{
\text{wall-disjoint pentagon train bulk + loaded returns + contact manifold}
\Longrightarrow
\text{collective movable-wall surplus paying a diameter cover}
}
\]
or an exact unit equilateral triangle.

High-value directions are:

1. construct a simultaneous deformation of the disjoint pentagon walls along contact-manifold/reciprocal coordinates that opens certified wall-safe capacity;
2. prove that a linear fraction of those pentagon walls must carry a quantitative refill surplus, not merely positive Oler residual;
3. couple their globally distinct loaded returns to an actual diameter vertex cover;
4. use long train separation and quadratic crossing mass to prove that the diameter cage cannot block all wall motions;
5. derive a consecutive near-square/oblique patch to which \`C-EMBEDDED-WALL-REFILL\` applies directly.

A theorem asserting universal fixed-wall refill from positive residual, near-triangularity, or quadratic wall population is false by the registered regressions.

The previous generic phrase “active-diameter feasibility” remains correct, but audit.54 makes the desired mechanism substantially more concrete: **certified collective wall surplus that pays an actual diameter cover**.

